                     fallback module via libpdx-cap M3-002).
  doc rm             remove (peer coreutil; shares
                     libpdx-audit + libpdx-elevate integration).
  doc mkdir          make directory (peer coreutil).
  doc libpdx-cap     capability manifest + narrowing.
  doc libpdx-audit   audit-journal client library.
  doc libpdx-elevate elevate broker client library.
  doc pdx-undo       undo-record replayer (R51).

.TOPIC history
.HEAD HISTORY
  R49-R50   design filed at design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.7
            in the paideia-os repo; issues #1-#16 filed against
            paideia-os/mv covering M1-M5.
  R50 M1    same-dir rename skeleton (issues #1-#3, LANDED
            2026-08-21).
  R50 M2    cross-dir + cross-device + signed-inode preservation
            (issues #4-#7, LANDED 2026-08-21).
  R50 M3    MoveRecord[] schema + libpdx-audit + PdxFS undo +
            libpdx-elevate (issues #8-#11, LANDED 2026-08-22).
  R50 M4    TXN-abort + undo replay + shape-smoke (issues
            #12-#14, LANDED 2026-08-22).
  R50 M5    dual-signed release + .pdxdoc + mirror push
            (issues #15-#16, this release, 2026-08-22).
  Enh v1.x  stack-frame fix (#17), libpdx-audit AuditClient wire-up
            + deps.list correction (#24), --verbose long spelling +
            false -v/-i claims stripped (#22), stale schema/undo
            magic reconciliation (#25), --dry-run TXN gate (#23).

.TOPIC bugs
.HEAD KNOWN LIMITATIONS
Every Pdxfs::* trampoline in this release is an M2 STUB (returns
0 or 1 without issuing a syscall). Live TXN dispatch lands with
the R42 PdxFS v1 substrate in the paideia-os kernel; the mv
binary is source-complete + audit-complete + undo-complete at
this release, but the QEMU acceptance smoke (mv a b; pdx-undo;
ls) waits on R42 + shell.M5 + pdx-undo. See `tests/README.md`
for the live-harness runbook and the fault-injection extension
that lands as a Round-2 amendment when R42 closes.

There is no `_start` frame in this tree (mv.ENH-002, #18): mv is a
set of well-formed modules, not yet a runnable program. There is no
cwd-relative path resolution (mv.ENH-003, #19). An existing dst is
silently overwritten with no record of what was destroyed -- the
undo record cannot recover a clobbered destination either, since it
only restores the moved file to its original name (mv.ENH-004, #20).
The multi-source form `mv f1 f2 ... dir/` is not implemented
(mv.ENH-011, #27). These are open issues tracked against the
Enhancement v1.x milestone, not regressions in this release.

.TOPIC author
.HEAD AUTHOR
